## 🔍 Pipeline Architecture & Explanation

The workflow script in [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../.github/workflows/ci.yml) automates build, lint, and test validation on every code change:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Push / Pull Request to main] --> B[Trigger GitHub Actions]
    B --> C[Matrix Build: Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12]
    C --> D[Set Working Directory to finance_app]
    D --> E[Checkout Code & Restore Pip Cache]
    E --> F[Install Requirements]
    F --> G[Run Flake8 Syntax & Error Check]
    G --> H[Run Black Code Formatting Check]
    H --> I[Run Unittest Suite in TestingConfig Mode]
    I --> J[Report Workflow Status Pass / Fail]
```

### Key Components

| Block / Feature | Rationale |
| :--- | :--- |
| **`on: push / pull_request`** | Runs tests automatically on every commit to main or when opening a pull request. |
| **`working-directory: finance_app`** | Ensures all `pip` and `python -m unittest` commands run seamlessly inside the app directory structure. |
| **`matrix: python-version: [3.10, 3.11, 3.12]`** | Verifies compatibility across modern Python runtimes simultaneously. |
| **`cache: 'pip'`** | Speeds up workflow execution by caching downloaded packages across runs. |
| **`TestingConfig` Mode** | Sets `FLASK_ENV: testing`, running all 39 tests against an isolated in-memory SQLite database. |

