## 🚀 How to Enable & Verify on GitHub

### Step 1: Commit and Push to GitHub
Run the following commands in your shell to push the new workflow to your repository:

```bash
git add .github/workflows/ci.yml
git commit -m "ci: add GitHub Actions workflow for linting and unit testing"
git push origin HEAD
```

After pushing your branch, open or update a Pull Request targeting the `main` branch to trigger the CI workflow.

### Step 2: View Workflow Runs on GitHub
1. Navigate to your repository on **GitHub.com**.
2. Click on the **Actions** tab at the top of the repository page.
3. Select the **CI Pipeline** workflow from the left sidebar.
4. Click on the latest run to inspect the status of the Python 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12 jobs in real time!

